  "nameConventions": [
    "Use the catalog spelling: ids and names map one to one.",
    "Names start in lower case unless they begin with a proper noun (93 % of official names): onions, Parmesan in one piece (32% fat).",
    "Counted items use the plural catalog name even for 1: garlic cloves, eggs (medium).",
    "Qualifiers go in parentheses (fat content, egg size, flour type: 18 % of official names) or after a comma (black, ground, dried, untreated: 27 %).",
    "To-taste items: purpose suffix in the name and an empty amount, for example 'salt to taste', 'pepper to taste' or 'butter for the tin'.",
    "Equipment listed as an ingredient (tins, baking paper, kitchen string) goes into an EQUIPMENT group and never counts toward the bowl mass."
